1
00:00:01,568 --> 00:00:04,628
Blue Cop's Special Training!

2
00:00:10,291 --> 00:00:11,762
Blue Cop!

3
00:00:12,836 --> 00:00:15,217
How about you ditch this piece of scrap metal,

4
00:00:15,217 --> 00:00:18,949
and form a new team with me, Jun?

5
00:00:21,489 --> 00:00:23,367
Alright! Heeheehee!

6
00:00:23,367 --> 00:00:24,402
H-Huh?!

7
00:00:36,706 --> 00:00:37,893
Wait Jun!

8
00:00:37,893 --> 00:00:39,295
Please! Don't leave me!

9
00:00:39,295 --> 00:00:40,572
Jun!!

10
00:00:41,823 --> 00:00:42,843
What are you talking about?

11
00:00:43,914 --> 00:00:46,276
I'm not going anywhere.

12
00:00:46,276 --> 00:00:47,987
You even had a nightmare...

13
00:00:47,987 --> 00:00:50,438
the defeat must have come as a shock.

14
00:00:50,438 --> 00:00:52,740
Lighten up, Blue Cop!

15
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:55,206
Next time, you'll definitely defeat that guy in one blow!

16
00:00:55,206 --> 00:00:58,887
With my current strength... There's no way I can beat Wild Guardy.

17
00:00:58,887 --> 00:01:01,710
Don't doubt yourself like that!

18
00:01:01,710 --> 00:01:03,597
We'll work hard together to become even stronger!

19
00:01:03,597 --> 00:01:05,236
Become stronger?

20
00:01:07,188 --> 00:01:09,198
So it's time for some special training?

21
00:01:09,198 --> 00:01:10,944
Special training?

22
00:01:10,944 --> 00:01:13,248
Yes. Just leave it to me.

23
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,129
Ok!

24
00:01:16,935 --> 00:01:18,700
Special training for Blue Cop?

25
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:24,361
Yeah. Uncle Edo said he's going to set up a new spot for some special training. He's been working on some new equipment for it.

26
00:01:24,361 --> 00:01:27,310
Really? Wow! I wanna come check it out!

27
00:01:27,310 --> 00:01:30,786
I heard it will be ready today. Should I ask?

28
00:01:30,786 --> 00:01:31,510
Blue Cop!

29
00:01:31,798 --> 00:01:32,468
Jun.

30
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:34,414
Is the special training ready?

31
00:01:34,414 --> 00:01:35,527
Yeah.

32
00:01:35,527 --> 00:01:38,549
-It's almost done. We'll be starting the training soon.
-No, no. That goes over here!

33
00:01:39,133 --> 00:01:42,168
Alright! Keep it up! I'll be there soon.

34
00:01:42,168 --> 00:01:44,264
What are you guys so excited about?

35
00:01:44,264 --> 00:01:45,658
Waaah!!

36
00:01:45,658 --> 00:01:47,668
U-Uh, it's nothing...

37
00:01:48,496 --> 00:01:50,140
...hey guys...

38
00:01:50,341 --> 00:01:54,293
Jun, did you forget Crest invited us to his house today?

39
00:01:54,293 --> 00:01:56,325
Aha... I kinda did...

40
00:01:56,325 --> 00:01:59,262
You're not trying to skip out on it, are you?

41
00:01:59,262 --> 00:02:01,751
Actually, I do have something, uh...

42
00:02:01,751 --> 00:02:03,813
Pretending to be busy, huh?

43
00:02:03,813 --> 00:02:06,989
If it's nothing urgent, why don't you just drop by for a little while?

44
00:02:06,989 --> 00:02:09,514
You said you wanted to try out the latest VR game.

45
00:02:09,514 --> 00:02:11,806
Uh... If that's alright?...

46
00:02:11,806 --> 00:02:13,973
Of course, come on.

47
00:02:15,454 --> 00:02:16,919
Let's go.

48
00:02:18,518 --> 00:02:20,783
This will be fun!

49
00:02:31,175 --> 00:02:33,574
Woah...

50
00:02:33,574 --> 00:02:35,783
This place is huge!

51
00:02:36,706 --> 00:02:38,396
Welcome back, master.

52
00:02:38,396 --> 00:02:39,901
You have a robot at home?!

53
00:02:39,901 --> 00:02:41,349
His name is Sebastian.

54
00:02:41,349 --> 00:02:43,348
Pleasure to meet you all.

55
00:02:43,348 --> 00:02:47,389
He's an all-purpose robot. He can do everything from chores to security.

56
00:02:47,389 --> 00:02:49,348
And your parents?

57
00:02:49,348 --> 00:02:51,908
They're often overseas for work.

58
00:02:52,765 --> 00:02:56,459
So, Crest... you live here all by yourself?

59
00:02:56,459 --> 00:02:59,265
Well, yes... but it doesn't get lonely.

60
00:02:59,265 --> 00:03:02,450
After all, I've made so many new friends around here.

61
00:03:02,450 --> 00:03:05,551
I-I'm happy for you.

62
00:03:10,676 --> 00:03:11,288
Ah!

63
00:03:12,139 --> 00:03:13,906
This is the last one.

64
00:03:14,459 --> 00:03:17,295
Alright, we're finally ready now!

65
00:03:17,295 --> 00:03:20,336
Huh? What are you going to do with these sticks?

66
00:03:20,336 --> 00:03:22,114
You'll find out soon.

67
00:03:22,114 --> 00:03:24,438
Blue Cop! To the center, please!

68
00:03:24,438 --> 00:03:25,304
Yes, sir!

69
00:03:25,651 --> 00:03:26,401
Huh?

70
00:03:27,596 --> 00:03:28,984
Is this good?

71
00:03:28,984 --> 00:03:29,768
Yep.

72
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:31,943
Alright, then!..

73
00:03:35,411 --> 00:03:38,593
Woah...

74
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:52,935
This training module will teach you how to dodge enemy attacks and to land counterattacks.

75
00:03:52,935 --> 00:03:56,128
I made it by modifying a virtual hologram game.

76
00:03:56,128 --> 00:04:00,679
But it's synced to your neural network, so it will still pack a punch if you get hit.

77
00:04:00,679 --> 00:04:02,235
Alright, are you ready?

78
00:04:02,235 --> 00:04:03,429
Of course.

79
00:04:04,340 --> 00:04:05,590
Here we go!

80
00:04:17,379 --> 00:04:19,206
That looked like it hurt.

81
00:04:19,985 --> 00:04:21,656
The effects are stronger than expected.

82
00:04:21,656 --> 00:04:22,730
Are you okay?

83
00:04:23,127 --> 00:04:24,379
I'm okay.

84
00:04:24,379 --> 00:04:25,579
Let's go again!

85
00:04:32,310 --> 00:04:34,191
No chance, kid!

86
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:40,521
Haha! Way to go, Vance! Yeah!

87
00:04:40,521 --> 00:04:42,370
Get him, Theo!

88
00:04:45,896 --> 00:04:48,850
Haha, you'll never beat me!

89
00:04:48,850 --> 00:04:51,132
Jun. Want to give it a go?

90
00:04:51,132 --> 00:04:52,490
Alright!

91
00:04:52,490 --> 00:04:54,680
I'll make sure to avenge Theo.

92
00:04:56,668 --> 00:04:59,499
Not you... or you...

93
00:04:59,499 --> 00:05:01,197
Aha! I'll pick this one!

94
00:05:14,766 --> 00:05:18,559
Will this training even work for mechanical lifeforms like us?

95
00:05:18,559 --> 00:05:21,514
Hard to say. Looks like a waste of time.

96
00:05:21,514 --> 00:05:25,802
It's not a waste of time! Hard work and perseverance always pays off!

97
00:05:29,826 --> 00:05:30,675
Again!

98
00:05:30,836 --> 00:05:31,646
Again!

99
00:05:32,230 --> 00:05:36,129
Haha! No matter how many times you try, I'll still kick your butt!

100
00:05:36,129 --> 00:05:39,273
That was just a warm up! I'll beat you this time!

101
00:05:39,273 --> 00:05:42,466
Alright! I'll beat you until you collapse from exhaustion!

102
00:05:42,466 --> 00:05:45,591
Ugh. What are they getting so worked up over?

103
00:05:45,591 --> 00:05:46,887
At least they're having fun.

104
00:05:47,956 --> 00:05:49,899
How ya like this?!

105
00:05:55,817 --> 00:05:56,401
Again!

106
00:06:00,437 --> 00:06:01,278
Again!

107
00:06:04,271 --> 00:06:05,709
Again!

108
00:06:08,370 --> 00:06:10,175
Grr... Again!

109
00:06:10,521 --> 00:06:12,451
Grr... Again!

110
00:06:14,603 --> 00:06:17,473
That's enough "agains" for now. Go take a break.

111
00:06:17,615 --> 00:06:20,146
Let me show you how it's done!

112
00:06:20,146 --> 00:06:21,742
Alright.

113
00:06:24,269 --> 00:06:25,622
Alright, let's go!

114
00:06:30,326 --> 00:06:32,132
I wasn't ready!

115
00:06:37,468 --> 00:06:38,326
Come on!

116
00:06:38,326 --> 00:06:39,951
Seems like he's still not ready.

117
00:06:39,951 --> 00:06:44,401
Haha! He's running into every hit! That's got to be some kind of world record!

118
00:06:45,389 --> 00:06:48,550
If you calculate the course and speed of the attack-

119
00:06:48,550 --> 00:06:50,367
and respond a little before it lands...

120
00:06:50,367 --> 00:06:54,439
H-hey! Wait up! Augh...

121
00:06:54,439 --> 00:06:57,271
Ugh. This isn't helping at all.

122
00:06:57,271 --> 00:06:59,572
No. I think I've figured it out.

123
00:07:01,620 --> 00:07:03,213
Edo! Let's try one more time.

124
00:07:03,346 --> 00:07:04,853
Attack pattern?

125
00:07:04,853 --> 00:07:09,500
Mhm. Each robot character has its own attack pattern and timing.

126
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:12,704
Figure that out and you might be able to beat Vance.

127
00:07:12,704 --> 00:07:16,300
Heh! No amount of advice is gonna help this loser beat me!

128
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:17,884
Alright. Thanks.

129
00:07:25,524 --> 00:07:26,420
Again!

130
00:07:32,850 --> 00:07:34,192
It's working!

131
00:07:34,192 --> 00:07:35,769
I can get stronger!

132
00:07:36,814 --> 00:07:40,261
Well done! Just do as I showed you!

133
00:07:40,261 --> 00:07:43,151
I think the trick is to do the opposite of what you did.

134
00:07:43,151 --> 00:07:46,680
Seems like Blue Cop's reaction time has picked up!

135
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:49,754
Looks like he's predicting the attack pattern and moving preemptively.

136
00:07:53,807 --> 00:07:56,792
Hey! Why aren't the hits landing?!

137
00:07:57,531 --> 00:08:01,110
Grr... so that's how you wanna play?

138
00:08:03,163 --> 00:08:05,810
It's about time I get to use this!

139
00:08:12,149 --> 00:08:13,879
Huh? Hey...

140
00:08:13,879 --> 00:08:15,942
How did you get so big?!

141
00:08:15,942 --> 00:08:18,237
Get ready for my special move!

142
00:08:42,153 --> 00:08:43,375
Never!

143
00:08:43,375 --> 00:08:44,389
Never!-

144
00:08:44,912 --> 00:08:46,100
Give up!

145
00:08:49,793 --> 00:08:50,518
Huh?

146
00:08:51,163 --> 00:08:52,330
What is...

147
00:08:52,538 --> 00:08:53,820
This power?...

148
00:08:56,874 --> 00:08:58,129
Jun!
Blue Cop!

149
00:09:07,513 --> 00:09:08,888
Infinity...

150
00:09:08,888 --> 00:09:10,490
Force...

151
00:09:10,490 --> 00:09:11,767
Break!!

152
00:09:27,312 --> 00:09:28,928
Aw, come on!

153
00:09:30,211 --> 00:09:33,548
What was all that about?! Probably just dumb luck!

154
00:09:35,850 --> 00:09:37,870
Hey Jun. Could I have your watch?

155
00:09:37,870 --> 00:09:38,735
Augh?!

156
00:09:38,735 --> 00:09:41,182
Of course, I'm not expecting it for free.

157
00:09:41,182 --> 00:09:43,538
I'll trade you anything in this room for it.

158
00:09:43,538 --> 00:09:44,721
How about it?

159
00:09:44,721 --> 00:09:45,988
For real?

160
00:09:45,988 --> 00:09:47,855
Then can I have your TV?

161
00:09:47,855 --> 00:09:49,875
Can I have your robot?

162
00:09:49,875 --> 00:09:52,764
W-what are you talking about?

163
00:09:52,764 --> 00:09:54,769
That could be something important to Jun.

164
00:09:54,769 --> 00:09:57,110
It's up to Jun to decide if he wants to trade.

165
00:09:57,110 --> 00:09:59,480
So... what would you like?

166
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:01,697
Uhh...

167
00:10:01,697 --> 00:10:03,725
Sorry! I have to go now!

168
00:10:04,385 --> 00:10:06,408
T-Thanks for the game!

169
00:10:08,572 --> 00:10:11,269
And so... he just runs away.

170
00:10:14,456 --> 00:10:16,850
Blue Cop!

171
00:10:16,937 --> 00:10:17,576
Jun!

172
00:10:21,945 --> 00:10:25,666
I get it now! When our hearts join as one, we become stronger!

173
00:10:25,666 --> 00:10:28,600
So it's true. The voice from before... it was you.

174
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:32,375
It seems like the Metal Breath still holds a lot of secrets to be discovered.

175
00:10:32,375 --> 00:10:33,322
Hm.

176
00:10:33,322 --> 00:10:37,548
So when Jun and Blue Cop's feelings are connected, the power of his card grows...

177
00:10:37,548 --> 00:10:39,485
and new skills are unleashed.

178
00:10:39,485 --> 00:10:42,975
Then... that means we could also power up like Blue Cop.

179
00:10:42,975 --> 00:10:45,596
Alright! Let's start training together!

180
00:10:45,596 --> 00:10:49,149
It could be Wild Guardy or Heavy Iron... we can beat 'em all!

181
00:10:49,149 --> 00:10:50,639
Let's do it, guys!

182
00:10:50,869 --> 00:10:53,158
But... where's Uncle Edo?

183
00:10:55,825 --> 00:10:58,937
My storage room...!

184
00:11:03,729 --> 00:11:06,812
I really thought I had him right where I wanted.

185
00:11:06,812 --> 00:11:09,865
But I didn't manage to get the Metal Breath.

186
00:11:09,865 --> 00:11:11,758
I'm sorry, Wild Guardy.

187
00:11:11,758 --> 00:11:13,841
You do not have to apologize.

188
00:11:13,841 --> 00:11:18,538
The great Wild Guardy will take the Metal Breath with my own skill and prowess.

